The updated `pylint` target drops `PYLINTHOME` (previously pointing at `$(CURDIR)/.pylint-cache`). `.pylint-cache` is explicitly gitignored, which suggests the repo expects pylint’s cache to live there. Without `PYLINTHOME`, pylint will default to a user-level cache location, reducing reproducibility and potentially impacting CI caching/debuggability. Consider restoring `PYLINTHOME` (and any other required env) when invoking pylint.
```suggestion
	@mkdir -p .pylint-cache
	@PYLINTHOME="$(CURDIR)/.pylint-cache" uv run pylint -j 0 --fail-on E --fail-under 10 $(TARGET)
```
